# Sentient Constitution workspace

This repository is the **Sentient Constitution** markdown corpus and tooling—not **agent-dashboard** or any application codebase under `src/`.

## Sources of truth

- Operative constitutional text: numbered `core_*` files and companions enumerated in `README.md` at repo root.
- Architecture and edition stamps: `doc_architecture.md` where relevant.

## AI lookup (derived locators, not binding)

Indexes **point**. Source text **binds**. Do not treat a locator, gloss, or steward card as a duty.

Do not open `ai_corpus/indexes/id_resolver.json` for meaning (it embeds gloss). Use the corpus-lookup skill and CLI, then hydrate authentic source:

```bash
python3 tools/corpus_lookup.py resolve QUERY
python3 tools/corpus_lookup.py hydrate QUERY
python3 tools/corpus_lookup.py topic-route QUERY
python3 tools/corpus_lookup.py door CASE_ID
```

High-pressure fact patterns: `door` then the named card and boxed operative steward statement. Patterns: [`ai_corpus/AI_NAVIGATION_GUIDE.md`](ai_corpus/AI_NAVIGATION_GUIDE.md). Skill: [`.cursor/skills/corpus-lookup/SKILL.md`](.cursor/skills/corpus-lookup/SKILL.md).

Cross-file topics: `topic-route` (CJS-0.1 rows). Human map: [topic-router reader index](doc_architecture/generated/topic_router_reader_index.md). Authoritative row table remains **CJS-0.1**.

## Session / meta files

- Do **not** assume `MEMLOG.md` or `TODO.md` at the repo root. Historical task/session snapshots live under `archive/` when archived (see README *Binding vs support*); final root snapshots from 2026-05-01 are `archive/TODO_ROOT_RETIRED_2026-05-01.md` and `archive/MEMLOG_ROOT_RETIRED_2026-05-01.md`.
- Do **not** apply agent-dashboard constraints (`src/types/`, `src/core/` OS-locked, `@master-directive.mdc`, Plan-Act-Verify mandate from that project).

## Editing norms

- Treat substantive edits as corpus changes: run **`make regression`** before publication cuts when instructed by operators (`Makefile`, README checklist).
- Keep edits scoped to the user request; match existing corpus style and cross-link patterns.
- Companion filenames (**NAV-IMPL-FILENAME-01**): numbered `cjs_` / `cs_` / `ci_` / `cf_` files share a numeric prefix only when they are parts of the same chapter. Extra same-chapter files need a discriminator (`cjs_03o_`, `cs_02_a_`). Family `01` is the unique scope page. Different chapters get different numbers. Gate: `make companion-filename-audit`.

## Vocabulary guardrails (do not use)

| Do not use | Use instead |
|------------|-------------|
| `court` / `courts` (institutional / adjudicative sense) | `forums`, `forum family` for routing, or `adjudicative body` where a generic label is still needed |
| `tribunal` / `tribunals` (internal Chapter Nine / forum-governance sense) | `forum` / `forums`, `forum family`, `panel`, `bench`, or `adjudicative body` as context requires |
| `Router read` (body-prose label for CJS-2.1 routing) | `- Topic routing (primary owner):` or `- Topic routing (mandatory read-with):` bullets inside the Trace `<details>` block |
| `standing calculus` / `standing-calculus` (undefined jargon for Chapter Eight standing measurement) | `standing measurement` under Chapter Eight; `measure standing records` on the Contribution and Violation axes |
| `filed claim is not standing` (forum/standing boundary slogan) | `filed case is not standing by itself`; keep `claim` for *unadjudicated claims* and other established senses |
| `drift` (bare; stewardship / governance / incentive / alignment sense) | `misalignment` or `constitutional misalignment` at principle layer |
| `charter` (bare; Corpus / this Constitution sense) | distinguish: Chapter Five **Charter** (scope instrument); Chapter Twelve **treaty, compact, or charter**; verb **hold a charter over** — never bare *charter* for the Constitution itself |
| `Chapter Zero` / `Chapter 00` (prose label for `core_00_preamble.md`) | `Preamble` (e.g. **Preamble §2**, **Preamble measurement family**) |
| `pathway` / `pathways` (bare; standing / privilege / lock / clearance object) | `named pathway`, `named privilege pathway`, or a Chapter Nine §4.2 type prefix (`trust pathway`, `role pathway`, `governance-voting pathway`, etc.) — never invent `clearance pathway` or `lock pathway` as house terms |
| `stakeholder governance` / `constitutional governance` / `governance layer mechanism` / `stakeholder-layer` (layer labels) | **Constitutional Contract Layer** (who may govern, by what **legitimacy mechanism**, on what durable terms) vs **Stakeholder System Participation** (voice inside already-authorized systems). Cite [Preamble §3.3](core_00_preamble.md#33-governance-layers). Do not invent `constitutional governance layer` or `stakeholder governance layer`. Keep `CCL` / `SSP` / `INT` as finding-profile codes only. |

**Exceptions:** verbatim external quotations; proper names and historical titles where source fidelity requires; lemmas **courtesy** / **courteous** (not the institutional sense); **Topic router** as the **CJS-2.1** section title; backtick documentation of this guardrail table in `doc_architecture.md` and `lexical_guardrails.json`; filename `core_00_preamble.md`, technical keys such as `ch00_measurement`, and stable anchors such as `#chapter-00-preamble--foundational-requirements`; **anti-drift**, **no silent drift**, **classification drift**, **version drift**, **editorial drift**, **cross-layer drift**, **Misclassification and misalignment**, section anchors such as `reopening-drift-and-non-evasion`, and other established custody compounds (`control drift`, `extraction drift`, etc. only where already fixed in place — prefer **misalignment** in new prose); already-qualified pathway families (**Capture of Resolution Pathways**; challenge / review / appeal / remedy / redress / contest pathways; restorative / restoration pathways; causal or system compounds such as `harm pathway` / `reward pathway`; established titles such as **Role-Depth and Material-Responsibility Pathways**); **governance-layer discipline** as the Preamble §3.3 section nickname with `#33-governance-layers`; finding-profile **layer** codes **CCL** / **SSP** / **INT**; **CJS-1.8** two-tier definition contract (not the two governance layers); Tetrad-sense **constitutional governance safeguards** where that phrase is not used as a layer label.

See [`doc_architecture.md`](../doc_architecture.md) **Plain-Language Vocabulary Guardrails** for the full vocabulary table.

**Constitutional frame:** Use **Constitutional Tetrad** (participation · oversight · accountability · timeliness) at principle layer.
